  "goodToKnow": "Die Genossenschaft is a cooperative: eine Wohnungsgenossenschaft (housing co-op, offering cheaper long-term rentals), eine Energiegenossenschaft. Germany's cooperative movement goes back to Hermann Schulze-Delitzsch and Friedrich Wilhelm Raiffeisen in the 19th century; Volksbanken and Raiffeisenbanken are cooperative banks. In 2016 UNESCO added the cooperative idea, nominated by Germany, to its list of intangible cultural heritage. Members are Genossen."
